#! seed 1861
# Civil War Strategy: every entry of the Utility menu, then a game with what they set (QB64Rust's
# tools/screen/README.md, "Places and rules"). Vary Start first (it reads the configuration and the start again);
# Graphics four times round; sound on, the last Sounds entry (silent: under a script the game plays at volume 0); Display Very
# Slow, the other colors, Fast; Balance Rebel ++; End Cond time off and on; Random Events Esc, Neutral, OFF, Favor
# Rebels, Favor Union; Jan Campgn off; Realism off and on; Chk Links; History on; Aggress six times round; Side
# Rebel and back; 2 Player and back. Then END TURN by rules: in November 1861 the Rebels win on cities (the
# other colors, sound and history on), the Hall of Fame, Game Over, Quit. A run takes about 26 s: the notes take
# their time.

# The waits of the computer's turns: a space each; a Retreat menu: the city it starts on; a main menu: END TURN;
# the End Turn and End Game menus: Yes; the Options at the end: Quit this Game.
rule 1:R key space
rule 1:P key space
rule 1:B key space
rule 1:U key space
rule 1:K key space
rule 1:I key space
rule 1:N key space
rule 1:S key space
rule 1:H key space
rule 1:G key space
rule 1:F key space
rule 1:L key space
rule 2:M text e
rule 2:E text y
rule 2:R key enter
rule 2:O text q
# The title menu: Start NEW Game; March 1861, the main menu: UTILITY.
play until 2:V
digest
text s
# The scenario menu: the Standard Map.
play until 2:S
text s
play until 2:M
digest
text u
# Vary Start first: it reads the configuration again
prompt
text v
# Graphics four times round
prompt
text g
prompt
text g
prompt
text g
prompt
text g
# Noise: the last entry (its first character is a note): up from the first
prompt
text n
prompt
key up
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest
# Display: Very Slow, Reg Color, Fast
text d
prompt
text v
prompt
text d
prompt
text r
prompt
text d
prompt
text f
# Balance: Rebel ++
prompt
text b
prompt
text r
# End Cond: time off and on, out
prompt
text e
prompt
key enter
prompt
key enter
prompt
key esc
# Random events: Esc, which shows the setting in force (Favor Rebels); then Neutral, OFF, Favor Rebels
# (the second F, by arrows), Favor Union
prompt
text r
prompt
key esc
prompt
state
key space
prompt
text r
prompt
text n
prompt
key space
prompt
text r
prompt
text o
prompt
key space
prompt
text r
prompt
key up
prompt
key enter
prompt
key space
prompt
text r
prompt
text f
prompt
key space
# Jan Campgn, then Realism twice (the row below it)
prompt
text j
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter
prompt
key enter
# Chk Links, which goes to the main menu: UTILITY again.
prompt
text c
play until 2:M
digest
text u
# History on; Aggress six times round
prompt
text h
prompt
text a
prompt
text a
prompt
text a
prompt
text a
prompt
text a
prompt
text a
# Side: Rebel, and back to Union (each goes to the main menu)
prompt
text s
prompt
text u
prompt
text s
prompt
text u
# 2 Player, and back (the entry then reads 2 Player)
prompt
text 1
prompt
text 2
prompt
state
key esc
# Four turns: the main menu, END TURN (and Yes by the rule).
repeat 4
play until 2:M
digest
text e
end
# November 1861: the Rebels control 80 % of the cities; End Game (Yes by the rule), the Options: Quit.
play until 2:O
state
text q
# The Union Hall of Fame: the commander's name; Game Over; the title menu: Quit; END's key.
play until 4
state
text Grant
key enter
play until 2:V
state
text q
repeat space
